<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nuno Álvares Botelho</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1630</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nuno Álvares Botelho was a Portuguese naval commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> who briefly shared the government of Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. In 1629 he led the fleet that relieved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> from the great siege by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iskandar-muda">Iskandar Muda</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a>, destroying the Acehnese armada with help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a> and Patani. He was killed in 1630 in fighting off Jambi in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>.</p></div>
